continuing to be really ugly.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.160
Is there anything new going on you can tell
me about?

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:21.950
Well, I can definitely say, you know, during
the last election I live in a predominantly

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:27.280
Republican County and we had, you know, like
six voting places.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.910
It was very easy for you in a Republican part
of the state to get to get to vote and to

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.900
not have a long line it sounds like.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:35.900
Yeah.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.290
Oh, it it awfully.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:42.250
So just in a place where I both, there were
six functioning machines.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.250
Okay.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:50.190
You know, and we, we didn't, you know, we're
a small County, you know, we, we only have,

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:56.120
I would say less than 15,000 in our County
total.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.400
And you know, but I do know a few people that
have been bumped off.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.790
I personally haven't because I'm an avid boater.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:04.790
Right.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:10.340
You know, so I think they can't meet, even
though I'm sure they would love to, you know?

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:15.650
Well, the good news that is that if you live
in a red part of Georgia, you are going to

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.940
have problem voting in November.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.250
That's the good news, I guess.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.709
Ah, yes.

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:26.019
You know, I guess that's about the best you
can get from it.

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:27.019
Yeah.

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:28.019
All right.

00:03:28.019 --> 00:03:29.260
Tammy, really appreciate hearing from you.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.260
Yeah.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.260
It sounds like we're going to keep covering.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.260
All right.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.260
Thank you so much.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.870
